Zepi
====

Zepi is a Windows workspace built on the shoulders of other projects. What is used and under which
license is listed below.

Foundation
----------
- Zed — https://github.com/zed-industries/zed
  Copyright Zed Industries, Inc. Dual-licensed Apache-2.0 / GPL-3.0-or-later.
  Zepi is distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later (see LICENSE): it uses Zed code and its derivative
  overlay native/overlay/**.
- eido — https://github.com/tony3liu/eido
  The first Zed + pi pairing on Windows, from which Zepi descends (GPL-3.0-or-later).
- pi — https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono
  The agent and the ACP protocol, packages @earendil-works/pi-* (GPL-3.0-or-later), bundled in
  packages/.

Vendored document engines (keep their own licenses)
---------------------------------------------------
- gridcraft (xlsx) — https://github.com/storytold — MIT OR Apache-2.0
- deckcraft (pptx) — https://github.com/storytold — MIT OR Apache-2.0
- wordcraft (docx) — https://github.com/storytold — MIT OR Apache-2.0

License texts live in native/overlay/vendor/<project>/LICENSE-*.

Other components
----------------
- Node.js (deps/node) — MIT, https://nodejs.org
- CPython (deps/python) — PSF License, https://python.org
- Playwright Chromium (deps/browsers) — BSD-3-Clause (Playwright); Chromium is BSD-3-Clause plus
  the third-party licenses inside the Chromium distribution
- python-docx, openpyxl, python-pptx, pypdf, Pillow — MIT / BSD / Apache-2.0 (see their dist-info in
  deps/python/Lib/site-packages)
- Every other dependency — see Cargo.toml and package.json.

